Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:34:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 045/154] refactor: a platform seam for the window, proved on
 the traffic lights
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AtriumWindowPlatform is the interface the Atrium window will hold instead of
reaching for AppKit itself. Shaped like BrowserNativeWidget: pure virtual, no
platform type in the header, one mac-only implementation behind a factory.

The traffic lights go first because they are the hardest small block. The
collapse path does not just hide them - it fades them over the pane animation
and hides them for real only at the end, since a fully transparent control
still takes clicks, and it asks again at that moment because an expand can
land while the fade is in flight. SetWindowControlsVisible carries that as a
confirm_hide callback rather than flattening it to a boolean.

The second call site, the sidebar side switch, is the same operation with a
zero duration.

standardWindowButton no longer appears in atrium_browser_window.mm.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
